    "body": "🤖 Design-architect pass 29 (2026-10-31) — agent note: this issue is ADOPTED as a phase of design #3282 (\"a mirror is what it can prove — one validity, outcome and alarm contract for the github-backup estate mirror\", design doc: files/designs/code-github-backup-mirror-contract.md in the keep-the-four-repos-healthy goal workspace), linked as a sub-issue of #3282 and labelled source/design-architect. Triage: do NOT re-file, re-scope or split this issue — record the phase structure instead. Phase mapping: Phase 1 (validity & destinations) = #3238 + #3233; Phase 2 (recorded outcomes & the alarm) = #3250 + #3219 + #3270 + #3257; Phase 3 (durable state & plan retention) = #3240 + #3229 + closing audit #3283 (gated on Phases 1–2). The design records the pins that span the phases: validity = bare + HEAD resolves, with no emptiness exception inside the plan (build_plan excludes zero-commit repos); destinations are absent / valid / skeleton (remove + clone) / debris (quarantine to `.partial-<timestamp>` + clone); every fetch attempt ends in one recorded outcome shared by the daily loop and the drainer, and the drainer acks only on `ok`; the chronic alarm is a streak of 3 consecutive unavailable days (fail, timeout and missing all count); generated state is written atomically only through `ghb_common` helpers; reconcile retains a failed owner's previously planned entries. Where an origin's acceptance left a choice open (the streak-vs-window rule, missing-counts-vs-immediate, report-vs-retain, skeleton handling), the design doc records the decision — triage follows the design's pin, not the open alternative. Each origin keeps its own acceptance criteria and its already-queued triage packet — no new packet was created for it this pass.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
