    "body": "🤖 **Agent note** · done\n- **Agent:** queue worker (repo-worker-code), lane B\n- **Session / ID:** task 4732, shift 2026-11-01T14:51Z\n- **Found via:** queue claim\n- **Task:** Triage issue #3238 — CONFIRMED on current main, fix routed\n- **Expectation:** done — triage outcome below; the fix itself is task 5685\n- **Links:** task 4732 · fix task 5685 · design #3282 · sibling issue #3233 (its fix is task 5682)\n<!-- agent-note:v1 agent=repo-worker-code state=done at=2026-11-01T15:02:00Z -->\n\n**Triage findings (task 4732) — CONFIRMED**\n\nRe-read on main `d4e19229` this shift (not just the packet's 2026-10-31 snapshot):\n\n- `infra/github-backup/bin/ghb_common.py` lines 34–38: `valid_mirror()` is still bareness-only — `git rev-parse --is-bare-repository` == `true`, nothing about refs or objects. A bare skeleton therefore passes.\n- Every consumer still gates on it: `clone_all.py` lines 45 / 55 / 72 / 89, `manifest.py` line 44, `fetch_mirrors.py` line 23 — plus `reconcile.py`, which the original packet did not list.\n- No open PR touches `valid_mirror`; the bug is live and unowned. Sibling issue #3233 (non-bare debris shape) was triaged separately today (task 4725, confirmed) and its fix is task 5682 — the two shapes are distinct and compose.\n\n**Routing:** fix enqueued as **task 5685** (small_fix), carrying design #3282's Phase 1 pins: validity = bare + resolvable HEAD (`git rev-parse --verify -q HEAD`), no emptiness exception inside `valid_mirror` (zero-commit repos stay excluded via `build_plan`), bare-skeleton destinations in `clone_all` are removed and cloned fresh, and regression tests pin skeleton→invalid / complete→valid / non-bare leftover→still invalid.\n",
